spec/spec-process-protected-path-policy.md:197:Runtime Settings is the preferred first storage location because it keeps policy configuration in the Runtime Contract and avoids introducing a new file format before the matching and authorization semantics are stable.
spec/spec-process-protected-path-policy.md:212:- **INF-001**: Runtime Home - Stores Runtime Settings and Runtime State.
docs/agent-context/codex-loop-context-management.md:9:It is written as a planning artifact for Personal Symphony. It does not change the Runtime Contract yet. Any implementation that introduces new Runtime Settings, Runtime State files, or domain language should update `CONTEXT.md` and add an ADR under `docs/adr/`.
docs/agent-context/codex-loop-context-management.md:13:`codex-loop` does not implement full transcript compression in its harness. It keeps compact loop state in local JSON, then uses Codex lifecycle hooks to inject a new continuation prompt when Codex stops too early.
docs/agent-context/codex-loop-context-management.md:19:The strongest transferable idea for Symphony is not Codex global hooks. Symphony already owns the agent launch harness, Agent Worktrees, Runtime State, and Agent Prompt composition. The transferable idea is a bounded, deterministic context snapshot that is generated by the harness immediately before launching or retrying an agent.
