+CONTEXT.md:99:**Agent Context Snapshot**:
+CONTEXT.md:101:_Avoid_: full context, context compression, transcript replay
+CONTEXT.md:103:**Context Command**:
+CONTEXT.md:104:An optional stage-specific local command whose bounded stdout may supplement an Agent Context Snapshot.
+CONTEXT.md:366:- An **Agent Context Snapshot** is generated by the Symphony launch harness, not by global Codex lifecycle hooks.
+CONTEXT.md:367:- An **Agent Context Snapshot** supplements the **Agent Prompt**.
+CONTEXT.md:368:- An **Agent Context Snapshot** supplements **Stage Goal Handoff** when both are enabled.
+CONTEXT.md:369:- An **Agent Context Snapshot** must not replace the **Agent Prompt** or **Stage Goal Handoff**.
+CONTEXT.md:370:- Runtime Settings own operator-configurable **Agent Context Snapshot** and **Context Command** behavior.
+CONTEXT.md:371:- **Agent Prompt** composition owns **Agent Context Snapshot** prompt injection.
+CONTEXT.md:372:- **Runtime State** may expose live **Agent Context Snapshot** generation status.
+CONTEXT.md:373:- **Runtime Diagnostics** may store bounded, secret-free **Agent Context Snapshot** and **Context Command** metadata.
+CONTEXT.md:374:- A **Context Command** belongs to a **Stage Agent** mapping.
+CONTEXT.md:375:- A **Context Command** stdout may supplement an **Agent Context Snapshot**.
+CONTEXT.md:376:- A **Context Command** stderr and failures are **Runtime Diagnostics** by default.
+CONTEXT.md:377:- A **Context Command** failure must not retry task work by itself.
+CONTEXT.md:378:- Missing **Agent Context Snapshot** or **Context Command** settings preserve existing Runtime Contract behavior.
+CONTEXT.md:584:- "full context" and "context compression" were used broadly for launch-time context; resolved: use **Agent Context Snapshot** for bounded deterministic launch context and **Context Command** for optional operator-generated stdout.
+spec/spec-design-independent-stage-completion-review.md:18:The purpose is to evaluate a feature inspired by `codex-loop` goal confirmation without mixing it into deterministic Agent Context Snapshot work.
+spec/spec-design-independent-stage-completion-review.md:46:- **CON-001**: Completion Review MUST NOT be implemented in the same slice as Agent Context Snapshot or Context Command execution.
+spec/spec-design-independent-stage-completion-review.md:79:- **AC-005**: Given Agent Context Snapshot work is reviewed, When Completion Review is evaluated, Then the two features remain separate.
+spec/spec-schema-context-readiness-runtime-status.md:18:The purpose is to make Agent Context Snapshot and Context Command status visible without making context status a primary orchestration metric.
+spec/spec-schema-context-readiness-runtime-status.md:58:        "summary": "Context Command exited 1; prompt contains bounded warning.",
+spec/spec-schema-context-readiness-runtime-status.md:73:| `timed_out` | Context Command exceeded timeout. |
+spec/spec-schema-context-readiness-runtime-status.md:79:- **AC-002**: Given Context Command succeeds, When Runtime State renders, Then status is `succeeded`.
+spec/spec-schema-context-readiness-runtime-status.md:80:- **AC-003**: Given Context Command times out, When Runtime State renders, Then status is `timed_out`.
+spec/spec-schema-context-readiness-runtime-status.md:119:- Context Command succeeds with empty stdout.
+spec/spec-tool-stage-context-command.md:2:title: Stage Context Command
+spec/spec-tool-stage-context-command.md:12:This specification defines a stage-specific Context Command that can add bounded operator-provided context to the Agent Context Snapshot.
+spec/spec-tool-stage-context-command.md:14:Source issue: [#40 Run A Stage Context Command Before Agent Launch](https://github.com/MatheusBBarni/symphony-orchestrator/issues/40).
+spec/spec-tool-stage-context-command.md:29:- **Context Command**: A local command configured for a Stage Agent that receives structured context and returns prompt content on stdout.
+spec/spec-tool-stage-context-command.md:30:- **Agent Context Snapshot**: The deterministic prompt section that can include Context Command stdout.
+spec/spec-tool-stage-context-command.md:37:- **REQ-001**: Context Command configuration MUST be optional and stage-specific.
+spec/spec-tool-stage-context-command.md:47:- **CON-001**: Context Command execution MUST NOT allow cwd outside the Workspace Repository root or Agent Worktree.
+spec/spec-tool-stage-context-command.md:48:- **CON-002**: Context Command failures MUST NOT move a task to retry by themselves.
+spec/spec-tool-stage-context-command.md:70:  "kind": "Context Command Input",
+spec/spec-tool-stage-context-command.md:73:    "title": "Run A Stage Context Command Before Agent Launch",
+spec/spec-tool-stage-context-command.md:86:- **AC-001**: Given missing Context Command config, When dispatch runs, Then no command executes.
+spec/spec-tool-stage-context-command.md:88:- **AC-003**: Given command stdout, When prompt composition finishes, Then stdout appears in the Agent Context Snapshot within byte limits.
+spec/spec-design-built-in-agent-context-snapshot.md:2:title: Built-In Agent Context Snapshot
+spec/spec-design-built-in-agent-context-snapshot.md:12:This specification defines the built-in Agent Context Snapshot rendered into an Agent Prompt before Symphony launches a Stage Agent.
+spec/spec-design-built-in-agent-context-snapshot.md:14:Source issue: [#38 Inject A Built-In Agent Context Snapshot](https://github.com/MatheusBBarni/symphony-orchestrator/issues/38).
+spec/spec-design-built-in-agent-context-snapshot.md:18:The purpose is to provide deterministic, bounded launch context without relying on Codex lifecycle hooks or full transcript storage.
+spec/spec-design-built-in-agent-context-snapshot.md:25:- Context Command execution. Covered by issue #40.
+spec/spec-design-built-in-agent-context-snapshot.md:31:- **Agent Context Snapshot**: Bounded deterministic markdown appended to the Agent Prompt.
+spec/spec-design-built-in-agent-context-snapshot.md:78:## Agent Context Snapshot
+spec/spec-design-built-in-agent-context-snapshot.md:80:- Issue: #38 Inject A Built-In Agent Context Snapshot
