+spec/spec-architecture-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:12:This specification defines the accepted runtime semantics for Agent Context Snapshot and Context Command behavior in Personal Symphony.
+spec/spec-architecture-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:14:Source issue: [#37 Accept Agent Context Snapshot Runtime Semantics](https://github.com/MatheusBBarni/symphony-orchestrator/issues/37).
+spec/spec-architecture-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:24:- Implementing Context Command execution.
+spec/spec-architecture-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:38:- **Agent Context Snapshot**: A bounded, deterministic context section generated by the Symphony launch harness before agent launch or retry.
+spec/spec-architecture-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:39:- **Context Command**: An optional operator-configured local command whose bounded stdout may supplement Agent Context Snapshot content.
+spec/spec-architecture-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:43:- **REQ-001**: Agent Context Snapshot MUST be generated by the Symphony launch harness.
+spec/spec-architecture-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:44:- **REQ-002**: Agent Context Snapshot MUST be scoped to the active Workspace Repository.
+spec/spec-architecture-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:45:- **REQ-003**: Agent Context Snapshot MUST supplement, not replace, the Agent Prompt.
+spec/spec-architecture-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:46:- **REQ-004**: Agent Context Snapshot MUST coexist with Stage Goal Handoff.
+spec/spec-architecture-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:54:- **GUD-001**: Use precise names such as Agent Context Snapshot and Context Command instead of ambiguous phrases such as "full context."
+spec/spec-architecture-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:75:- **AC-002**: Given `CONTEXT.md` is reviewed, When Agent Context Snapshot and Context Command are used, Then the terms are defined there.
+spec/spec-architecture-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:76:- **AC-003**: Given Stage Goal Handoff is enabled, When Agent Context Snapshot is enabled, Then both mechanisms remain distinct and ordered.
+spec/spec-architecture-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:118:Agent Context Snapshot, when enabled
+spec/spec-architecture-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:137:- [Agent Context Snapshot Runtime Semantics ADR](../docs/adr/0019-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md)
+docs/adr/0019-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:1:# Generate Agent Context Snapshot in the Symphony launch harness
+docs/adr/0019-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:3:Personal Symphony needs bounded launch context for agents, but global Codex lifecycle hooks would make Workspace Repository behavior depend on user-level Codex configuration outside the Runtime Contract. Symphony will generate Agent Context Snapshot content in its own launch harness, scoped to the active Workspace Repository, and will not install or mutate global Codex hooks.
+docs/adr/0019-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md:5:Runtime Settings own operator-configurable context behavior, Agent Prompt composition owns prompt injection, Runtime State may expose live generation status, and ignored Runtime Diagnostics may store bounded secret-free metadata. Agent Context Snapshot supplements the Agent Prompt and coexists with Stage Goal Handoff; it does not replace either. Context Command stdout may supplement the Agent Context Snapshot, while stderr and command failures remain diagnostic by default.
 
-**Stage Goal Handoff**:
-A stage-specific Codex handoff that sets a Codex goal when Symphony launches an agent for that stage.
-_Avoid_: global goal mode, `/goal` setting, issue goal
-
-**Stage Goal Context**:
-The deterministic issue and stage data used as the Codex goal payload for a Stage Goal Handoff.
-_Avoid_: whole prompt, all context, goal message
-Set `"enabled": false` to use the single base `.symphony/prompt.md` for every issue.
